<title>USA: Marathon ups U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bbl.</title>
<headline>Marathon ups U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil, a unit of USX Corp, said Tuesday it raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents a barrel, effective September 10.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $22.50 a barrel, and West Texas Sour to $21.15 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $22.50 a barrel, and Oklahoma sweet is $22.50.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859-1620</p>
